# {{ s.name }} — Unity Moving Platform

**Variant:** `{{ variant }}`
**Speed:** `{{ "%.1f"|format(s.speed) }}`
**Carries rider:** `{{ s.carries_rider }}`

{{ s.description }}

## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/`.
2. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to the platform GameObject (it needs a
   physical, non-trigger collider so a rider can actually stand on it).
{% if variant in ("waypoint_pingpong", "waypoint_loop") %}
3. Create an empty GameObject named `{{ s.waypoint_parent_name }}` with one
   empty child per stop, in order (EntitySpawner emits one of these
   automatically when the schema names a waypoint container).
{% elif variant == "oscillate" %}
3. No extra setup — it oscillates around its own starting position.
{% elif variant == "falling" %}
3. Tag your player `{{ s.target_tag }}`.
{% endif %}

## Behaviour

{% if variant == "waypoint_pingpong" %}
Travels to each child of `{{ s.waypoint_parent_name }}` in order at
**{{ "%.1f"|format(s.speed) }} m/s**, then reverses direction at the ends
(optionally pausing **{{ "%.1f"|format(s.wait_time) }}s** at each stop).
{% elif variant == "waypoint_loop" %}
Travels to each child of `{{ s.waypoint_parent_name }}` in order at
**{{ "%.1f"|format(s.speed) }} m/s**, then wraps back to the first
(optionally pausing **{{ "%.1f"|format(s.wait_time) }}s** at each stop).
{% elif variant == "oscillate" %}
Slides back and forth **{{ "%.1f"|format(s.oscillate_distance) }}m** along its
own **{{ s.oscillate_axis|upper }}** axis, no waypoints needed.
{% elif variant == "falling" %}
Static until a `{{ s.target_tag }}` stands on it; drops (collider + renderer
disabled) after **{{ "%.1f"|format(s.fall_delay) }}s**, then resets to its
start position after **{{ "%.1f"|format(s.respawn_delay) }}s**.
{% endif %}
{% if s.carries_rider %}
Whatever is tagged `{{ s.target_tag }}` and standing on it moves with it
(parented by delta-position, not Transform re-parenting, so it works the same
whether the platform uses 2D or 3D physics).
{% endif %}
